        "key": "e8",
        "n": 8,
        "kind": "exercise",
        "q": "What is a Gaussian mixture? What tasks can you use it for?",
        "a": "A Gaussian mixture model (GMM) is a probabilistic model that assumes that the instances were generated from a mixture of several Gaussian distributions whose parameters are unknown. In other words, the assumption is that the data is grouped into a finite number of clusters, each with an ellipsoidal shape (but the clusters may have different ellipsoidal shapes, sizes, orientations, and densities), and we don't know which cluster each instance belongs to. This model is useful for density estimation, clustering, and anomaly detection."
